{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0\fmodern Consolas;}}\f0\fs18 ==========================================================\par
 HS_LP FOREST ESSENTIALS \u8212? Low Poly Forest Pack  (v1.0)\par
==========================================================\par
\par
131 stylized low-poly forest assets: 44 unique tree species\par
(19 deciduous, 13 conifer, 9 character, 3 fruit/tropical),\par
4 saplings, water set (pond, stream, waterfall, lily pads,\par
reeds, water plants) and a full forest floor: rocks, logs,\par
bushes, grass, ferns, mushrooms, flowers and ground details.\par
\par
QUICK START\par
-----------\par
1. Drag prefabs from  HS_LowPoly/ForestEssentials/Prefabs/\par
   into your scene. Everything is prefixed P_HS_LP_.\par
2. Open  Scenes/HS_LP_ForestEssentials_Demo  to browse every\par
   asset laid out by category.\par
\par
TECHNICAL\par
---------\par
- ONE material (M_HS_LP_Palette) + one 256x224 palette\par
  texture (T_HS_LP_Palette, Point filter, no mips) for the\par
  entire pack -> minimal draw calls, great for mobile.\par
- ~30k triangles for ALL 131 assets (trees 300-1,200 tris,\par
  props 20-330 tris).\par
- Real-world scale, base-center pivots, clean HS_LP_ naming.\par
- Lightmap UVs generated on import (static-friendly).\par
\par
VERTEX COLORS (texture-free workflow)\par
-------------------------------------\par
Every mesh ALSO carries vertex colors identical to the\par
palette. Shaders/HS_LP_VertexColor.shader (+ material\par
M_HS_LP_VertexColor) renders the pack with zero textures\par
(URP shader: main light + ambient + shadows, matte).\par
\par
RENDER PIPELINES\par
----------------\par
Materials target the Universal Render Pipeline (URP) --\par
the default pipeline for Unity 6 projects. They use\par
URP/Lit with smoothness 0.\par
- Built-in RP: select M_HS_LP_Palette and M_HS_LP_Ground\par
  and switch their shader to "Standard" (the palette\par
  texture slots straight in; set Smoothness to 0). The\par
  vertex-color shader is URP-only.\par
- HDRP: switch the two materials to HDRP/Lit and reassign\par
  T_HS_LP_Palette as Base Map.\par
The single flat palette texture makes any conversion\par
lossless.\par
